Reason: Checking song durations one by one is tedious. A more efficient approach is to select all songs, add them to the playlist, then check the total duration. If it exceeds 45-50 minutes, I can remove songs. If it's under, I need to plan differently. Let me first exit selection mode and take a different approach - I'll select all songs first and add them to the playlist, then review.

Actually, the best approach is to use "Select all" from the overflow menu to select all songs, then add them all to the playlist and check total duration. Let me click More options and Select all.

